# Nest CLI for service structure

This is a **NestJS** app, not Next.js. When adding or reshaping Nest layers (module, controller, service, interceptor, pipe, filter, guard, DTO, resource), **do not hand-create the files**. Use Nest CLI.

```bash
npx nest g module <name>
npx nest g controller <name>
npx nest g service <name>
npx nest g interceptor <name>
npx nest g filter <name>
npx nest g pipe <name>
npx nest g guard <name>
npx nest g class dto/<name> --flat --no-spec
```

- Prefer `npx nest` so we do not require a global `@nestjs/cli`.
- Pass `--no-spec`: this repo has no unit-test suite yet.
- For DTO/class names that include a dot (`create-order.dto`), also pass `--flat`, otherwise Nest creates `dto/create-order.dto/create-order.dto.ts`.
- After generate, wire the class into the existing module/providers if the schematic did not.
- Do not invent a parallel folder layout; keep generated code under `src/` as Nest places it.
- Hand-edit only after the schematic has created the file (business logic, OpenAPI alignment).
- `nest g resource` is allowed when adding a full CRUD resource; still `--no-spec`, then trim unused methods to match `openapi/openapi.yaml`.
